  Copyright Mike Bostock. ISC licence. https://d3js.org

foldkit-flow takes its design from xyflow. React Flow and Svelte Flow are bindings over
@xyflow/system. foldkit-flow is a third binding: it drives the framework-free controllers
of that package (pan and zoom, drag, handles, minimap, resizer) from Foldkit Mounts and
uses its edge-path and graph utilities. xyflow asks its users to keep the attribution link
or to support the project; foldkit-flow therefore shows a link to https://xyflow.com in the
corner of the canvas by default, and an application can turn it off (see README.md, "Credit").

The repository, not the package, also holds files copied from other repositories. Those
copied from Apache-2.0 repositories (tsukuri-labs/tsukuri, tsukuri-labs/studio,
phibkro/vektorprogrammet-reimagined, phibkro/pg-txmode) keep the Apache-2.0 licence and the
headers that name their source; the licence text is LICENSES/Apache-2.0.txt, and
PROVENANCE.md lists every copied file with its source and licence. The MIT licence of this
project does not relicense them. None of them is in the npm package.

Two files of the example app come from the Foldkit template (create-foldkit-app, MIT,
